1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,461
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:09,009
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,635
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,016
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:18,893
[Atoy] <i>You were my mother's best friend.</i>

7
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:20,854
[Atoy] You deceived her before,

8
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:22,939
and now you're deceiving me every day

9
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:24,649
whenever you see my face.

10
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:26,776
How can you do that, Godmother?

11
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:30,321
Is my suspicion about you right?

12
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,490
I'm the product of their betrayal.

13
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:34,576
[Atoy] <i>You're still making</i>
<i>a fool of me up to now!</i>

14
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:35,660
[sobs]

15
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:38,496
[Atoy] <i>Ibyang is the only one</i>
<i>who truly loves me!</i>

16
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,457
She's the only genuine person in my life.

17
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:41,708
[Martina, in English] So, it's confirmed?

18
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:42,876
Sister Norma is still alive?

19
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:44,377
[Mongki, in English] <i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

20
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,463
<i>My man confirmed it.</i>

21
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:51,050
<i>And he overheard that they're meeting</i>
<i>someone to talk to Atoy.</i>

22
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:52,886
[in English] Hello, Sister Norma.

23
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:54,304
[in English] Remember me?

24
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:56,931
I was thinking of Master Grumpy.

25
00:00:57,015 --> 00:01:00,310
If that happens, I'll probably leave him.

26
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:03,021
The child… Where is she?

27
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:07,358
[stammers] Ame is with Ibyang!

28
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:09,611
[Ame] <i>I brought Ibyang with me.</i>

29
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:11,446
She wanted to see Sister too.

30
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,948
[in English] Is something wrong, Martina?

31
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:15,158
[in English] I'm just really happy that

32
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:16,367
she's gonna meet her parents
for the first time.

33
00:01:16,451 --> 00:01:19,579
[in English] I mean, you know me.
I love a family reunion story.

34
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,831
Doesn't seem like it.

35
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:24,417
Are you being fake with me?

36
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:25,585
It's crazy!

37
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:27,420
Our meeting place was so far,

38
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:30,006
and Sister Norma didn't even show up.

39
00:01:30,089 --> 00:01:32,175
Now I can't contact them--

40
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,344
[Ame] <i>Miss, why? Did something happen?</i>

41
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,804
[Red] <i>We need to get ahead of Atoy.</i>

42
00:01:35,887 --> 00:01:37,680
<i>He must not know that Ibyang</i>
<i>is his daughter.</i>

43
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:39,974
While you haven't met your parents yet,

44
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,226
can you…

45
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:42,185
PREVIOUSLY

46
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,812
Can you stay here again?

47
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,396
I'll think about it.

48
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,815
Are you still mad at me?

49
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,149
Just kidding!

50
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:50,360
[Ibyang] <i>Me? Mad at you?</i>

51
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:51,361
[music fades]

52
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:57,450
I'll take Red outside.

53
00:01:57,534 --> 00:01:58,409
[in English] Just get the car.

54
00:01:58,493 --> 00:01:59,869
[in English] Yes, ma'am.

55
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:07,085
Have you thought of a way?

56
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:10,713
How do we get Ibyang from Atoy?

57
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:16,761
We need to find someone who can pretend
to be Ibyang's real mother.

58
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,513
[suspicious music playing]

59
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,014
An actress?

60
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:24,060
[in English] Something like that, but…

61
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,020
she has to be on our side.

62
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:29,315
[music swells]

63
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:30,275
[music fades]

64
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:34,904
[suave theme music playing]

65
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:48,001
[gunshots]

66
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:50,295
[clacking]

67
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:52,380
[snipping]

68
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:55,341
[music swells]

69
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,554
[music fades]

70
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:01,389
Are you ready, children?

71
00:03:01,472 --> 00:03:02,307
Yes!

72
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:06,769
Remember, watch and listen to our story.

73
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:13,151
In a faraway forest lived a poor princess!

74
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:17,697
She had a mother who was sick,

75
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:22,994
and one day, she found her mother at home!

76
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:26,039
Mom, I'm here!

77
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:29,125
- [pensive music playing]
- [gasps]

78
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,335
Mom?

79
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:31,753
- [gasps]
- [kids giggling]

80
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:32,921
Mom!

81
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:34,088
Mom?!

82
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:35,048
Mom!

83
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:36,925
Mom, wake up!

84
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:38,343
Wake up, Mom!

85
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:39,510
[children laugh]

86
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:42,680
Don't leave me!
We still have so many dreams.

87
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:44,224
You really left me for that?

88
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,308
[Martina, in English] Why? It-It's--

89
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:46,309
[in English] It's ridiculous.

90
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:48,394
- She's like crazy.
- Mom!

91
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,354
- [children laughing]
- [sobs]

92
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:51,606
Who did this to you, Mom?!

93
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:53,191
Mom, wake up, Mom.

94
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:56,819
[Charmi] The poor princess noticed
something strange!

95
00:03:56,903 --> 00:04:01,866
There was a bite and two small marks

96
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,535
on her dead mother's neck!

97
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:09,415
Like a vampire's bite!

98
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:11,167
- [roars]
- [screams]

99
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:13,878
[roaring]

100
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:17,257
[children laughing]

101
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:23,179
[Olga] I know who did this.

102
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,681
Svetlana!

103
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,600
Svetlana!

104
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:29,686
Face me!

105
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:32,021
I'm not afraid of you!

106
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,148
[deep breath]

107
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,400
Smoke, hurry.

108
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:37,568
And suddenly there was smoke!

109
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:41,489
[audience laughing]

110
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,992
And suddenly there was smoke!

111
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:45,785
Mars, hurry up.

112
00:04:45,868 --> 00:04:46,828
Suddenly there's smoke, Mars.

113
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:48,621
And suddenly there was smoke!

114
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:50,748
- [inaudible]
- [grunts]

115
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:52,583
And suddenly there was smoke!

116
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:55,753
[imitates fizzing sound]

117
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:57,964
[sneaky music playing]

118
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:01,050
Then thunder and lightning,

119
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:03,636
and suddenly appeared…

120
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,722
Svetlana!

121
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:10,310
[cackling]

122
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:15,273
[audience laughing]

123
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:17,400
[Svetlana roars]

124
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:22,947
[Charmi] But the poor princess
did not surrender!

125
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:26,159
She was ready to fight!

126
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:27,368
[sneaky music playing]

127
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:29,078
I'm not afraid of you!

128
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:30,997
Prepare yourself!

129
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,333
[grunts]

130
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:36,711
- [imitates whooshing sound]
- [quirky stinging]

131
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:41,049
[audience laughing]

132
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:45,470
And Svetlana did not back down!

133
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:49,140
She wore her black cape

134
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:54,520
and unleashed her powerful… hair!

135
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,147
- [grunts]
- Then she screamed!

136
00:05:56,230 --> 00:06:02,361
[screaming]

137
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:05,823
[grunting and groaning]

138
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:09,744
The poor princess's power was strong!

139
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:13,664
Svetlana was defeated in battle.

140
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:14,999
[quirky stinging]

141
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:19,087
Darkness ended, and goodness prevailed!

142
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,589
That woman might work for our plan.

143
00:06:21,672 --> 00:06:24,467
[Martina, in English] What?
We need a serious actor for that.

144
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:26,385
[in English] Not some clown.

145
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,013
[in English] Look. Trust me on this.

146
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:32,016
She looks okay.

147
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:34,352
[Martina, in English] Okay.

148
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:37,855
[Charmi] And that's the end of our story!

149
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,732
[audience cheering, clapping]

150
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:41,859
[Charmi] Let's give her
a round of applause, children!

151
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:44,237
[audience cheering, clapping]

152
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:49,450
Tet, add 3K more!

153
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,245
Come on. What I did earlier was hard.

154
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:53,746
You saw it, right?

155
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,873
My gums hurt from those vampire fangs!

156
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:58,000
[Olga sighs] Unbelievable.

157
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,919
Sis, we're just a volunteer group,

158
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:02,964
and that's all the budget we have
for storytelling sessions.

159
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:06,008
Besides, a parent complained earlier.

160
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:08,678
Why was there a vampire killing a mother?

161
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:10,555
They said their child
might have nightmares.

162
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:13,766
And there's no vampire
with an aswang mother!

163
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,435
- Gosh!
- What's this?

164
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:18,229
So… exaggerated.

165
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:21,899
You know, they asked
for fantasy action drama, right?

166
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:24,360
If it's fantasy, anything goes!

167
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:26,070
Gosh, stop it, Tet!

168
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:27,989
[Tet] Just change it next time.

169
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:31,200
[Olga] Tet, add 3K to our talent fee.

170
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:34,078
If not, I'll tell your boss that

171
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:39,500
the receipts you're reimbursing
for volunteers' food are fake.

172
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,043
- [Tet] What?
- Oh, wow!

173
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:42,211
Oh, what?!

174
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:43,754
[in English] Girl… [scoffs]

175
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:45,840
Don't test me. I'll really do it.

176
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:48,092
I'm not a doctor, huh.

177
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:50,970
But I know the things you've been
"doctoring" for a long time.

178
00:07:51,053 --> 00:07:54,682
- What, girl? What? Huh?
- [Charmi] Whoa! So that's how it is?

179
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:58,936
[Charmi] Yes, that's how it is.

180
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:01,814
Sis, you only need 3K.

181
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,232
That's 6K already!

182
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:05,651
Oh, why? Touch-move!

183
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:06,944
Stop complaining.

184
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:08,488
[Olga] Fine.

185
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,406
- Wait, I need to answer this.
- [phone rings]

186
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:13,576
- This Tet.
- See?

187
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:15,286
- That's how it works.
- Just a little push--

188
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:17,455
- Oh, there.
- It's 8K now.

189
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:18,498
Nice.

190
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:21,667
We have money for food now, right?

191
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:22,752
[in English] Hi, there.

192
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:24,337
[in English] I saw your acting earlier.

193
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,796
- Oh.
- [in English] You're very good.

194
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,840
Oh, not really.

195
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:29,217
- [roars]
- [Martina chuckles]

196
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,093
- [Martina, in English] Exactly.
- [in English] Thank you!

197
00:08:32,136 --> 00:08:33,888
[in English] Can I have
your contact details?

198
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,598
[in English] I might have
an acting gig for you.

199
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:37,391
[in English] Yes, ma-- Yes, ma'am.

200
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:39,393
I have a set card here.

201
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,686
I'll send it to you.

202
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:42,355
Oh, just give me your number.

203
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:44,815
- Here.
- [in English] Thank you.

204
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:47,068
Here's my calling card.

205
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:48,152
[in English] Thank you!

206
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,821
[in English] Um, I'll call you later?

207
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:53,449
[in English] You think that maybe you'll…
you'll be free to meet us?

208
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:57,078
Yes, ma'am! I'll cancel
my pedicure for you.

209
00:08:57,161 --> 00:08:58,412
- [in English] You can also, um…
- [in English] Yes, ma'am.

210
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:01,749
- bring your friend.
- Hmm. [in English] Thank you, ma'am!

211
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:02,833
[in English] Thank you.

212
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:03,876
[in English] Thank you, ma'am!

213
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,086
- [in English] See you later.
- [in English] Thank you.

214
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:07,338
[exclaiming]

215
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:10,049
- [pleasant music playing]
- [both scream]

216
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:12,969
We're amazing!

217
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:15,471
[exclaiming]

218
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:16,764
Amazing!

219
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:18,391
- Really!
- [exclaims]

220
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:19,725
You know, wait.

221
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,394
Could she be

222
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:23,104
a Hollywood producer?

223
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:24,313
Oh, shucks.

224
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:27,608
[in English] Oh my God. Oh my God!

225
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:28,818
Meryl Streep.

226
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:32,238
Girl, get ready because…

227
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:35,157
Olga Bonifacio is here.

228
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:38,536
[exclaiming]

229
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:40,746
[Charmi] It hurts, friend.

230
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:41,956
Hey, really!

231
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:44,041
We're so lucky!

232
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:47,962
[music fades]

233
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:58,055
[Martina clears throat]

234
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:00,224
[in English] Good afternoon.

235
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:01,809
[in English] I'm Olga Bonifacio.

236
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,312
[in English] Olga, for short.

237
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:06,647
[in English] Hello, judges.

238
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:08,232
[in English] I am Charmielyn Sanchez.

239
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:09,483
[in English] Charmi, for short.

240
00:10:10,484 --> 00:10:13,404
Olga, I'll give you a scene.

241
00:10:13,487 --> 00:10:15,406
I just want to see how you'll act it out.

242
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:16,741
G, Director!

243
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,909
[in English] Game, um…

244
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:20,661
What kind of scene do you want?

245
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:26,792
Um, let's say you gave up
your child for adoption,

246
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:29,378
then after a long time you meet again,

247
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:32,006
and you want to reunite.

248
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:34,300
How will you talk to her?

249
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:36,385
How will you introduce yourself?

250
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:37,511
Show us.

251
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:39,180
I'll just internalize, Director.

252
00:10:39,263 --> 00:10:41,265
Wait. Wait, wait.

253
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:42,516
[suspicious music playing]

254
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,769
[sighs]

255
00:10:47,396 --> 00:10:48,773
[sighs]

256
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,691
Do you want me to cry, Director?

257
00:10:51,525 --> 00:10:53,486
Which side do you want?

258
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:57,031
Oh, do you want me to be doing something?

259
00:10:57,114 --> 00:10:58,741
Like sweeping…

260
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:00,159
Just do it.

261
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:02,119
[Red] What?

262
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:09,877
[rousing music playing]

263
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:15,883
[melodramatic music playing]

264
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:18,344
My child!

265
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,179
[sobs]

266
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:21,847
My child…

267
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:25,434
It's me.

268
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:27,645
It's me, your mama.

269
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,192
[sobs]

270
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:35,152
I missed you so much.

271
00:11:35,236 --> 00:11:38,447
[sobbing]

272
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:40,783
Forgive me.

273
00:11:42,701 --> 00:11:45,704
Please forgive me for giving you up.

274
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,373
I didn't want to.

275
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:49,625
But I want to make it up to you.

276
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:54,338
I want to make it up to you
if you'll let me.

277
00:11:55,297 --> 00:11:56,674
[music fades]

278
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:57,800
[in English] Cut.

279
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:03,055
- How was it?
- [mid-tempo rock music playing]

280
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:04,640
Send the other one home.

281
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:05,808
[in English] What do you mean?

282
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:07,184
[in English] We need her.

283
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:10,312
Olga can't just show up suddenly.

284
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:11,397
[in English] She needs to be endorsed.

285
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,940
[music fades]

286
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:14,358
How?

287
00:12:14,442 --> 00:12:16,694
Sister Norma's niece already called Ame.

288
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:18,779
[in English] We just need
to follow through with that.

289
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:22,992
We need somebody to play Faye,
Sister Norma's niece.

290
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,578
[in English] Got it?

291
00:12:25,661 --> 00:12:26,871
[in English] Yes.

292
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:31,292
- [mid-tempo rock music playing]
- [inaudible]

293
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:32,209
‪[music concludes]

294
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:38,048
[muffled chattering in the distance]

295
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:42,595
Ame, take care of Atoy, okay?

296
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:46,223
Sometimes he doesn't eat properly.

297
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:49,310
Don't worry, Miss Cita.

298
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:52,396
I'll find a way for you
and Atoy to talk again,

299
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,939
so you can go back to how you were before.

300
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:57,860
That might not happen anymore.

301
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:00,613
He sees me differently now.

302
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,156
And don't force it.

303
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:05,451
What's important is he's not alone.

304
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,745
He has you and Ibyang.

305
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,665
It's just sad what happened to you.

306
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:15,628
You've become like a mother to him.

307
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:18,589
[melancholic music playing]

308
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:25,513
[phone ringing]

309
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:29,308
Hello?

310
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:30,851
[Charmi] <i>Ms. Ame!</i>

311
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:32,269
[suspicious music playing]

312
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:33,229
Faye?

313
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:34,271
Oh, sorry!

314
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:36,774
I wasn't able to meet you last time
at the hospital.

315
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:39,068
Something happened to Sister Norma.

316
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,237
She had to go to the province.

317
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,988
But she left instructions!

318
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:45,574
Why does your voice sound different?

319
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:49,453
Ah, it's because, um3

320
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:50,871
[clears throat] I was sick--

321
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:55,417
[coughing]

322
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:56,585
[in English] Sorry.

323
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,128
I was sick then,

324
00:13:58,212 --> 00:14:00,548
so maybe my voice sounded different.

325
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:02,091
Um…

326
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:06,178
Um, Ms. Ame, where can we meet Ibyang?

327
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:10,474
So we can bring her mother to you.

328
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:12,101
Huh?

329
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:14,103
You'll bring her later?

330
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:16,313
What's her name?

331
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:18,232
Olga Bonifacio.

332
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,985
Okay, Ms. Ame.

333
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,820
Let's just chat.

334
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:24,113
[in English] See you!

335
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:28,200
[music swells]

336
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:33,706
- You're good too, Charmi.
- Yes.

337
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:36,667
So later, you'll tag team with Olga.

338
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:39,128
- She's the mother, and you're…?
- Faye!

339
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,256
Sister Norma's niece.

340
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:46,135
Right? I memorized the profile
you gave me.

341
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:48,387
[in English] Good!

342
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:50,097
- [in English] Thank you.
- [chuckles]

343
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,807
[rousing music playing]

344
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,100
Hey, Ibyang.

345
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:55,853
Did you tidy your room?

346
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,438
Make sure, okay.

347
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:59,189
Change the bed sheets too!

348
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:01,275
Don't come down if it's not neat!

349
00:15:01,358 --> 00:15:03,319
[Ibyang] Okay, Tatoy!

350
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:06,697
[phone ringing]

351
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:08,532
Yes, Sir Mike?

352
00:15:10,784 --> 00:15:13,370
Yes, Sir Mike.
Uh, the suit you ordered is ready.

353
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:15,372
You can pick it up anytime.

354
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:17,875
[in English] Okay, thank you.

355
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:25,090
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

356
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:36,477
[Olga] Is this right?

357
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:37,811
- [music fades]
- [mutters]

358
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,480
[Faye] Is the child here now?

359
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:41,482
[Charmi] Eh…

360
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:44,568
That's what Ame said in her text.

361
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:47,196
[in English] Delfin's Tailoring Shop.

362
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:48,572
There it is.

363
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:51,075
Hmm, you know…

364
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:54,161
This place looks familiar.

365
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:57,665
[sneaky music playing]

366
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,501
I borrowed a suit here before!

367
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:02,836
Oh no.

368
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:05,005
Could it be…

369
00:16:05,881 --> 00:16:08,842
Oh. Why are you smiling like that?

370
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,096
[clicks tongue]

371
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:13,097
Hey!

372
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,723
Don't think about that now!

373
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:16,684
Let's focus here!

374
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,102
We can't mess this up.

375
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:20,187
- We need to do great.
- Yes.

376
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:23,899
Honestly, I'm nervous
about this acting gig.

377
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:25,734
Because why won't they explain

378
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:28,529
why you need to get the child?

379
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:31,991
Never mind.

380
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,492
We're getting paid.

381
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:34,535
It's a big amount too!

382
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:35,703
If not for this gig,

383
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:37,204
we'd have nothing now, right?

384
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:39,581
[Olga] Did we pass?

385
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:41,709
Are we accepted?

386
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:44,837
[in English] Yes? Yes?!

387
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:47,339
[whooping, exclaiming]

388
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,091
[playful music playing]

389
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:52,428
- I told you, right?
- Told you, yes!

390
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:54,513
- [giggles]
- [whoops]

391
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:56,348
I'm amazing!

392
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:57,766
[Olga, in English] I'm so proud of myself.

393
00:16:58,350 --> 00:16:59,393
[sighs] What is this?

394
00:16:59,476 --> 00:17:01,854
When does the taping start?

395
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:04,023
I-Indie? Indie film?

396
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:06,442
[gasps]

397
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,068
[in English] Broadway!

398
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:09,611
[Martina, in English] Can you just…

399
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:12,197
shut it for just a minute?

400
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,365
[in English] Sorry.

401
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,950
[Martina, in English]
This is not an ordinary role.

402
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:17,745
[in English] You have to be
extremely convincing.

403
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,955
[in English] Improvisation skills
are a must.

404
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:24,043
Also, this will take a lot of your time.

405
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:26,879
[in English] So, listen very,
very carefully. Okay?

406
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,589
[in English] Okay. Um…

407
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:31,842
If ever, how much is my talent fee here?

408
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:35,512
[in English] For you, 200,000 a month.

409
00:17:36,555 --> 00:17:39,058
[Martina] Plus miscellaneous expenses.

410
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,017
[in English] Okay?

411
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,685
[in English] This is
an indefinite contract.

412
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:45,647
We'll decide when to terminate
your services.

413
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:48,233
[in English] Your friend here
will get 50,000

414
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:51,028
for playing a supporting role.

415
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:52,780
[in English] One-time.

416
00:17:52,863 --> 00:17:54,740
[in English] Okay! Game, game.

417
00:17:54,823 --> 00:17:56,658
What do I need to do?

418
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,453
[sighs]

419
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:04,917
[music fades]

420
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:07,920
She's Ibyang.

421
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:11,507
You'll pretend to be her mother,

422
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:13,842
take her in.

423
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,677
You'll keep her in your care,

424
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,554
treat her like your real child.

425
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:21,100
We'll tell you when to stop pretending.

426
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,560
Ah, like reality TV?

427
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,813
[Charmi] Hmm. Mm-hmm.

428
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:27,648
Exactly, but…

429
00:18:27,731 --> 00:18:31,777
no TV, no cameras watching you.

430
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,738
[in English] This is real life.
This is a real kid.

431
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:37,116
Only you are fake.
Only you are pretending.

432
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:38,117
[in English] Don't worry.

433
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,661
We'll supply ou with all the information
and background that you need.

434
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:41,870
There are just some people

435
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:45,499
that you need to watch out for
who might suspect you.

436
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:46,917
[in English] That's it.

437
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,002
Can we start from the top?

438
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,838
[sneaky music playing]

439
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:52,673
Oh, just kidding.

440
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,134
Just a joke.

441
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:56,468
[chuckles]

442
00:18:58,762 --> 00:19:00,013
- Okay. Come on.
- [in English] Oh, game.

443
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:01,682
Let's change clothes. Where's my costume?

444
00:19:01,765 --> 00:19:03,142
Here. Let's get ready.

445
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:04,226
[in English] Okay. Okay.

446
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:07,437
[in English] Olga Bonifacio. Listen to me.

447
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:10,107
You love Ibyang.

448
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:12,401
You're her mother, okay?

449
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:16,280
You love her because you need money.

450
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:17,865
[in English] Okay?

451
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:19,575
- [in English] Let's do it.
- [in English] Okay.

452
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:21,160
Oh, give it to me.
It's there, on the side.

453
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:22,619
Here, put on your shoes first.

454
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:23,912
Give me the shoes.

455
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:30,878
[blabbering]

456
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:32,129
[in English] One Mississippi.

457
00:19:32,212 --> 00:19:33,547
[in English] One Mississippi.

458
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:38,093
[sharp exhale]

459
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:41,263
[Olga] Hey.

460
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:42,723
Just put it there.

461
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,435
Hello?

462
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:48,061
Good day!

463
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,314
[Atoy] What is it? You're here to have
something tailored?

464
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:55,903
Yes. I'd like a women's suit made.

465
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:59,198
[Atoy] Ah, okay. Just a moment.
I'm finishing something.

466
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,699
Just relax first.

467
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:07,456
[sneaky music playing]

468
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:08,498
Oh.

469
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:10,918
There's a child here?

470
00:20:11,668 --> 00:20:12,878
[Atoy] Child?

471
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:15,589
Yes, my assistant.

472
00:20:15,672 --> 00:20:17,341
[Olga] Ivy Santos.

473
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,677
[Atoy] Do you know Ibyang?

474
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,555
Ah, I just saw it on her ID.

475
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,599
- [Atoy] Mm-hmm.
- Where is she?

476
00:20:28,518 --> 00:20:30,520
[Atoy] I thought you came for tailoring?

477
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,481
Why are you looking for her?

478
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:36,026
[suspicious music playing]

479
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:40,322
Yes, I'm here for tailoring.

480
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:42,115
You're so grumpy.

481
00:20:42,199 --> 00:20:45,786
I was just curious
about your assistant, wow.

482
00:20:46,578 --> 00:20:47,788
- [sighs]
- [Atoy] Just a moment.

483
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:50,165
I'm finishing something here.

484
00:20:54,878 --> 00:20:56,463
[gasps, then squeals]

485
00:20:56,546 --> 00:20:58,048
[Charmi] Hey, oh--

486
00:20:58,131 --> 00:20:59,967
- Did Red send you?
- [gasping]

487
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,343
Huh? Who sent you?

488
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:02,344
- Help! Hey!
- [shrieking]

489
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:03,679
- [gasps, grunts]
- Hmm?

490
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:07,641
[grunting and groaning]

491
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:11,353
Ms. Ame, help Olga!

492
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:13,146
- Olga?
- [Olga] Atoy!

493
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:15,649
Oh, Atoy!

494
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:18,360
She's Ibyang's mother!

495
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:23,156
[rousing music playing]

496
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:27,953
‪[clicks tongue]

497
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:31,373
You're an animal, Atoy.

498
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:35,419
[mysterious music playing]

499
00:21:38,505 --> 00:21:40,966
I already spoke to Olga's friend.

500
00:21:41,049 --> 00:21:42,968
They're with Atoy now.

501
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:47,264
[suspicious music playing]

502
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:48,890
What?

503
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:51,143
So, you're Ibyang's mother?

504
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:53,687
- Ame, what's this?
- [sighs]

505
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:54,688
What?

506
00:21:54,771 --> 00:21:56,440
Why are you only showing up now?

507
00:21:57,107 --> 00:21:59,109
[in English] Sorry! Okay?

508
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:00,777
I just found out she's here!

509
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:02,070
I've been searching for so long!

510
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:04,072
Because you left her!

511
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:05,449
[sneaky music playing]

512
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:07,784
Ah, wait. Wait a minute.

513
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:08,869
What's going on?

514
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:10,454
[in English] Uh, excuse me.

515
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:14,291
I'm Faye, Sister Norma's niece.

516
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:16,668
She already went back to the province.

517
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:19,838
But she's happy
I brought Ibyang's mother here.

518
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:22,841
Atoy, she is the one I told you

519
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:25,343
we were supposed to meet
yesterday with Ibyang.

520
00:22:25,427 --> 00:22:26,303
Her?

521
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:28,722
Wait.

522
00:22:28,805 --> 00:22:30,098
How did you meet?

523
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:33,435
[whimsical music playing]

524
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:38,065
How did you meet?!

525
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:42,986
[sneaky music playing]

526
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:47,699
Brother, one please. The 20-peso one.

527
00:22:53,288 --> 00:22:54,247
‪[indistinct chattering]

528
00:22:59,127 --> 00:23:00,504
Henry!

529
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:02,589
- Oh, here's the money I owe you.
- [in English] Thank you.

530
00:23:02,672 --> 00:23:03,757
[in English] Thank you!

531
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,592
I'll pay the rest later, okay?

532
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:09,096
- Uh, brother.
- Hmm?

533
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:10,514
I just want to ask.

534
00:23:10,597 --> 00:23:14,518
Is the church with the image
of San Antonio de Padua nearby?

535
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:16,812
[Nestor] Ah, yes. It's close…

536
00:23:17,437 --> 00:23:19,397
Second corner, turn right.

537
00:23:20,023 --> 00:23:22,859
- Here, straight, then right?
- Right, straight ahead.

538
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:25,028
Why? Did you lose something?

539
00:23:25,112 --> 00:23:26,154
Eh…

540
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:32,077
Well, my love life
has been missing for a long time.

541
00:23:33,203 --> 00:23:35,288
I haven't had a boyfriend
in ages, brother.

542
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:37,916
Mm-hmm. So, I'll just leave it to prayers.

543
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:39,835
[both chuckling]

544
00:23:40,794 --> 00:23:44,339
So, what are you looking for
in a man? Maybe…

545
00:23:44,422 --> 00:23:45,966
Maybe our patron will have
a hard time with what you want.

546
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,468
- Oh no! It's simple.
- [laughs]

547
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:49,928
Simple.

548
00:23:50,011 --> 00:23:51,763
Of course, handsome.

549
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,598
- That's important, right?
- [Nestor] Correct.

550
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:57,185
- Tall. Dresses well.
- [quirky sting]

551
00:23:58,603 --> 00:24:01,898
You know, even if he's not rich,
that's fine with me.

552
00:24:01,982 --> 00:24:05,068
- And I like someone who looks grumpy
- [chuckles]

553
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:06,611
but is kind in real life!

554
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,113
[both chuckling]

555
00:24:08,196 --> 00:24:09,197
That's simple indeed.

556
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:10,407
- [quirky sting]
- [chuckles]

557
00:24:11,074 --> 00:24:12,868
Uh, my advice to you…

558
00:24:13,451 --> 00:24:16,371
Pray, and it will come.

559
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:19,249
- [in English] Prayers.
- Thanks.

560
00:24:19,332 --> 00:24:20,333
Thank you. Drink that. It's good.

561
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:22,085
- [in English] Thank you!
- Henry, later, okay!

562
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:26,339
[gasps]

563
00:24:26,423 --> 00:24:28,216
- Oh, what's that?!
- [Atoy, in English] Oh, sorry.

564
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,844
- [in English] Sorry. Sorry.
- What's that?

565
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:33,805
[romantic music playing]

566
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:35,765
[Atoy] Sorry. Sorry, sorry.

567
00:24:36,892 --> 00:24:37,726
[chuckles softly]

568
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:39,895
Sorry, because--

569
00:24:46,943 --> 00:24:48,528
It splashed.

570
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:50,947
- [in English] Sorry.
- [in English] Thank you.

571
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:53,116
- [chuckles softly]
- [in English] Sorry.

572
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,784
[in English] Oh my God!

573
00:24:54,868 --> 00:24:56,745
[in English] San Antonio de Padua,
thank you.

574
00:24:56,828 --> 00:24:58,038
You're so fast!

575
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:00,248
What's your name?

576
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:01,833
Ah, Atoy.

577
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:03,293
- Yes.
- [giggles]

578
00:25:03,376 --> 00:25:06,254
Atoy, do you have a girlfriend?

579
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:09,257
- None, none.
- None, ah.

580
00:25:09,966 --> 00:25:12,385
Well, if you're looking, um…

581
00:25:12,469 --> 00:25:14,804
Here, call me at this number.

582
00:25:16,473 --> 00:25:18,308
- [titters]
- [Atoy] Oh, okay--

583
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:19,434
If I get a boyfriend,

584
00:25:19,517 --> 00:25:21,561
I'll make myself available for you, okay?

585
00:25:21,645 --> 00:25:23,647
Wow, jeez.

586
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,190
You're too fast, miss.

587
00:25:25,273 --> 00:25:26,816
Don't you want us
to get to know each other first?

588
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,443
What do you want to know?

589
00:25:30,403 --> 00:25:31,613
Uh…

590
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,660
[music fades]

591
00:25:36,743 --> 00:25:40,789
[electronic blipping]

592
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:49,381
She's Olga. She's your mother.

593
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:51,716
[lively theme music playing]

594
00:25:52,425 --> 00:25:54,219
What about Brother Atoy?

595
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:56,054
[T-Bak] Then he'll just go solo in life?

596
00:25:56,137 --> 00:25:57,514
There's still Sis…

597
00:25:57,597 --> 00:25:58,890
Ame and Miss Cita.

598
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:00,642
Oh, but Cita's gone!

599
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:01,977
She resigned!

600
00:26:02,060 --> 00:26:04,980
Why is your mother
not there anymore, Karla?

601
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:09,317
I know that you'll be happier there,

602
00:26:09,818 --> 00:26:12,320
that your identity will be complete.

603
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,364
I'll miss you.

604
00:26:14,447 --> 00:26:16,074
Eventually, the child
has to be disposed of.

605
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,409
What do you mean, disposed of?

606
00:26:17,492 --> 00:26:20,036
She can be included in a shipment or…

607
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:22,580
get rid of her, so there's no trace.

608
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:24,916
[Emerson] <i>'Toy, I just want to know.</i>

609
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,961
<i>Has the DNA test result</i>
<i>been emailed to you?</i>

610
00:26:28,044 --> 00:26:29,337
<i>It's being sent now.</i>

611
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,880
UP NEXT

612
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:32,215
Yes, it's here.

613
00:26:32,299 --> 00:26:36,803
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

614
00:26:36,886 --> 00:26:38,805
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

615
00:26:38,888 --> 00:26:40,432
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
